WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.190 --> 00:00:03.531
If you want to know more about some of the
ties among the first three Child’s Play

00:00:03.540 --> 00:00:07.920
movies that you might not have known about,
then stick around to end of this video.

00:00:12.060 --> 00:00:16.190
We pick up right where we left off -- yeah
I’m just jumping into this -- at the factory

00:00:16.190 --> 00:00:20.880
from the end of Child’s Play 2, only a lot
of time has passed and it’s now shut down.

00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:24.930
The opening titles are very Halloween, but
instead of showing the decomposing pumpkin

00:00:24.930 --> 00:00:29.210
in reverse, we see the plastic melting in
reverse, and also being infused with Chucky’s

00:00:29.210 --> 00:00:30.250
cursed blood or whatever.

00:00:30.250 --> 00:00:34.329
I don’t know, this is the dumbest method
of resurrection for Chucky yet -- and I think

00:00:34.329 --> 00:00:35.329
that’s saying a lot.

00:00:35.329 --> 00:00:38.700
We find out that the company behind the Good
Guy dolls are thinking about bringing them

00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:42.360
back, and Mr. Sullivan, our buddy from the
second movie makes the final call.

00:00:42.360 --> 00:00:44.859
He has a conversation with one of the other
executives.

00:00:47.880 --> 00:00:50.260
“Well, if there’s nothing else, I’m
gonna get going.”

00:00:52.680 --> 00:00:55.060
“It’s just my wife’s expecting me.

00:00:55.070 --> 00:00:56.719
It’s our anniversary.”

00:00:56.719 --> 00:01:00.620
This is a direct parallel to the executive
who gets killed early on in Child’s Play

00:01:00.620 --> 00:01:01.620
2.

00:01:01.620 --> 00:01:02.620
“The vodka.

00:01:02.620 --> 00:01:03.620
Oh the vodka, of course I remembered the vodka.

00:01:03.620 --> 00:01:06.660
Two week anniversary, you think I’d forget
the vodka?

00:01:06.760 --> 00:01:10.300
So apparently there’s also a cut scene from
that movie where he immediately calls his

00:01:10.300 --> 00:01:12.970
wife after that and tells her he’ll be home
late.

00:01:12.970 --> 00:01:17.120
So I guess the two-week anniversary is like
how long he’s been smashing his assistant.

00:01:17.120 --> 00:01:20.660
But back to Child’s Play 3. Looking around
Mr. Sullivan’s office, there are a few set

00:01:20.661 --> 00:01:23.920
pieces that foreshadow the events that would
later take place.

00:01:23.920 --> 00:01:27.910
For example, this ferris wheel precedes the
final sequence taking place at a fair.

00:01:27.910 --> 00:01:31.900
This toy army man is a hint that the movie
will take place in a military school.

00:01:31.900 --> 00:01:36.350
If we pause as the camera sweeps by Mr. Sullivan’s
computer, you may see a text document called

00:01:36.350 --> 00:01:39.650
Barclay.doc alongside some numerical information.

00:01:39.650 --> 00:01:43.390
This is the same computer that Chucky uses
to find Andy’s location, so it seems like

00:01:43.390 --> 00:01:46.480
the company may be keeping tabs on him to
make sure he doesn’t do anything else to

00:01:46.480 --> 00:01:48.520
possibly damage their profit lines any further.

00:01:48.520 --> 00:01:52.820
That might be the creepiest thing in the movie
actually, imagine this corporation secretly

00:01:52.820 --> 00:01:57.250
tracking your every move for 8 years after
one of their dolls tried to kill you.

00:01:57.250 --> 00:02:00.640
In the last two Things You Missed episodes,
I mentioned the potential mistake on the Good

00:02:00.660 --> 00:02:04.860
Guys boxes, where it said Play Partners Toys
instead of Play Pals Toys, which is the name

00:02:04.860 --> 00:02:05.840
of the company.

00:02:05.840 --> 00:02:09.090
In this movie though, there seems to be more
products with Play Partners listed on the

00:02:09.090 --> 00:02:12.400
box, so I’m starting to think maybe this was not
a mistake.

00:02:12.410 --> 00:02:15.580
Maybe Play Partners is the parent company
of Play Pals or something.

00:02:15.590 --> 00:02:19.560
Chucky attacks Mr. Sullivan using an army
of his own toys, a fitting death considering

00:02:19.560 --> 00:02:22.880
he knowingly put a dangerous product on the
market in the last movie.

00:02:22.880 --> 00:02:26.620
Chucky chokes him to death, and his line,
“just like the good old days,” is a reference

00:02:26.620 --> 00:02:30.430
to him being a criminal known as The Lakeshore
Strangler prior to the events of the first

00:02:30.430 --> 00:02:31.430
one.

00:02:31.430 --> 00:02:34.170
We catch up with Andy as he rolls into the
military school, which looks like it’s in

00:02:34.170 --> 00:02:36.020
Missouri based on this license plate.

00:02:36.020 --> 00:02:38.920
Too bad for Andy, because St. Louis is boring.

00:02:38.920 --> 00:02:40.880
“Who would want to play in St. Louis?

00:02:40.880 --> 00:02:41.950
So boring.

00:02:41.950 --> 00:02:43.550
So boring.”

00:02:43.550 --> 00:02:47.209
Speaking of boring, the newspaper article
that the Colonel has in Andy’s file is the

00:02:47.209 --> 00:02:51.290
most boring and vague article I’ve ever
read, and it actually just repeats the same

00:02:51.290 --> 00:02:53.060
paragraphs over and over.

00:02:53.060 --> 00:02:56.390
I guess when you force out three movies in
three years though, this is the kind of quality

00:02:56.390 --> 00:02:57.990
you get from your art department.

00:02:57.990 --> 00:03:02.210
That being said, there is something of note
in the headline text, which reads: “Deaths

00:03:02.210 --> 00:03:03.210
still unresolved.

00:03:03.210 --> 00:03:04.690
Mother under psychiatric care.”

00:03:04.690 --> 00:03:08.020
This suggests that although we may not have
seen it in the other movies, there may have

00:03:08.020 --> 00:03:11.950
been some uncertainty in the public eye about
whether Andy’s mom actually deserved to

00:03:11.950 --> 00:03:12.950
be institutionalized.

00:03:12.950 --> 00:03:16.480
If the case is still open, that means they
may still be investigating.

00:03:16.480 --> 00:03:20.152
Andy is forced to get his hair cut for military
school, and in the barber shop there are some

00:03:20.152 --> 00:03:22.700
cadets whose locks are on display on the wall.

00:03:22.700 --> 00:03:25.290
Many of their names are jokes or pop culture
references.

00:03:25.290 --> 00:03:31.120
I saw a Mr. Smells, Mr. Hurts, Stud, Wile
E. Coyote, Bruce Willis and Tommy Lee Jones.

00:03:31.130 --> 00:03:33.620
There’s also a dart board in the room behind
Sgt.

00:03:33.620 --> 00:03:34.620
Botnik’s head.

00:03:34.620 --> 00:03:38.681
This could be a symbol for him being Chucky’s
future target, especially considering the

00:03:38.681 --> 00:03:42.840
fact that Chucks has already used darts as
weapons earlier in the movie against Mr. Sullivan.

00:03:42.840 --> 00:03:46.780
The sergeant tells Andy about how the Romans
invented the military cut so that their enemies

00:03:46.780 --> 00:03:49.280
couldn’t grab ahold of it in battle and
slit their throats.

00:03:49.280 --> 00:03:52.739
The strategy didn’t really work out for
him though, because he later meets his fate

00:03:52.739 --> 00:03:55.870
when he gets his throat slit by Chucky while
trying to give him a buzz.

00:03:55.870 --> 00:03:59.849
As he’s getting his trim, a Good Guys episode
comes on the TV and it’s the same episode

00:03:59.849 --> 00:04:03.300
from the first movie; we get to see a little
more of it on camera this time around.

00:04:03.300 --> 00:04:05.760
TV: "We're back and we're better than ever."

00:04:05.900 --> 00:04:07.860
"No one will play with me."

00:04:07.960 --> 00:04:11.240
"Uh-oh, there's a friend in need."

00:04:12.420 --> 00:04:16.420
This kid Tyler even has a similar reaction
to Andy, when he first saw the commercial.

00:04:16.560 --> 00:04:19.940
Tyler: "Wooooowwwww!!!"

00:04:20.640 --> 00:04:22.120
Andy: "Wow!"

00:04:22.780 --> 00:04:23.640
Owen Wilson: "Wow."

00:04:23.800 --> 00:04:27.580
So Chucky ends up mailing himself to Andy,
but Tyler ends up opening the box instead.

00:04:27.590 --> 00:04:32.160
I have some serious questions about how Chucky
was able to wrap up this package if he

00:04:32.160 --> 00:04:33.900
was inside of it.

00:04:33.900 --> 00:04:36.430
And then put that package in the mail.

00:04:36.430 --> 00:04:37.430
And pay for postage.

00:04:37.430 --> 00:04:40.590
But let’s just ignore those things and get
to the part where Chucky reveals his true

00:04:40.590 --> 00:04:43.730
self to Tyler and tries to do the ritual to
possess his body.

00:04:43.730 --> 00:04:46.480
The Colonel shows up and interrupts things
by taking Chucky away.

00:04:46.480 --> 00:04:47.480
“I’ll be back.”

00:04:48.680 --> 00:04:50.780
I think this is kind of a Terminator reference.

00:04:51.180 --> 00:04:52.140
"I'll be back"

00:04:52.520 --> 00:04:56.030
Chucky and the Terminator are both kind of
robotic killers in a way -- the main difference

00:04:56.030 --> 00:04:58.090
being that Chucky is slowly turning human.

00:04:58.090 --> 00:05:01.580
Andy’s roommate Whitehurst tells Andy he
needs to unpack, which may or may not be an

00:05:01.580 --> 00:05:05.491
intentional reference to Mrs. Simpson telling
Kyle to unpack in the previous movie; but

00:05:05.491 --> 00:05:09.020
Andy unpacks his stuff and we see that he’s
got a magazine called Play Pen.

00:05:09.020 --> 00:05:13.130
It seems Andy has grown up and moved from
Play Pals to Play Pen, and the text on the

00:05:13.130 --> 00:05:16.940
front of the magazine says, “come play with
me,” just as the Good Guy box says, “hi,

00:05:16.940 --> 00:05:18.610
I’m a Good Guy, let’s play.”

00:05:18.610 --> 00:05:22.210
Andy is left alone in the room with Chucky,
but the drill leader, Shelton, barges in and

00:05:22.210 --> 00:05:25.850
steals the doll as a present for his younger
sister and Andy is finally smart enough now

00:05:25.850 --> 00:05:30.490
to know that most people will think he’s
insane if he tells them the truth about Chucky.

00:05:30.490 --> 00:05:34.280
So instead, Andy tries to warn Tyler that
Chucky will come after him, but not before

00:05:34.280 --> 00:05:37.919
the Colonel sees Chucky moving around and
has a heart attack as a result.

00:05:37.919 --> 00:05:39.919
Then Chucky slits the throat of the barber,
Sgt.

00:05:39.919 --> 00:05:41.780
Botnik, as I mentioned earlier.

00:05:41.780 --> 00:05:45.570
So it all comes down to this thing they do
called The War Games, which is basically capture

00:05:45.570 --> 00:05:47.040
the flag meets paintball.

00:05:47.040 --> 00:05:50.680
My parents always used to use military school
as a punishment threat whenever I got in trouble,

00:05:50.680 --> 00:05:53.680
like “you better be good or we’re gonna
have to send you to military school!”

00:05:53.680 --> 00:05:56.280
And I always thought that would have been
like the worst punishment you could get as

00:05:56.280 --> 00:05:59.320
kid, but judging from this movie it… looks
kind of fun.

00:05:59.320 --> 00:06:03.389
I mean you get to camp out and possibly command
your own little army unit with paintballs

00:06:03.389 --> 00:06:04.389
and walkie talkies.

00:06:04.389 --> 00:06:07.840
I’d take that over sitting in a classroom
and watching Bill Nye the Science Guy all

00:06:07.840 --> 00:06:08.840
day.

00:06:08.840 --> 00:06:12.040
But it’s all fun and games until Chucky
brings in… a real grenade?

00:06:12.040 --> 00:06:13.900
Why does the school even have this?

00:06:13.900 --> 00:06:16.240
It’s like the whole shock device from the
first one all over again.

00:06:16.480 --> 00:06:18.360
Also, what happened to Chucky’s teeth?

00:06:18.360 --> 00:06:21.420
Looks like that one lady I pointed out in
the Black Christmas episode.

00:06:23.180 --> 00:06:26.540
Anyway, after Chucky tries to kill them all
with the grenade and Whitehurst takes one

00:06:26.550 --> 00:06:29.120
for the team, Tyler realizes, “you know
what?

00:06:29.120 --> 00:06:30.610
Maybe this Barclay kid was right.

00:06:30.610 --> 00:06:33.360
Maybe this Chucky guy isn’t such a good
guy.”

00:06:33.360 --> 00:06:35.780
I mean, he is technically a Good Guy…

00:06:35.780 --> 00:06:36.960
Just forget I said that...

00:06:36.960 --> 00:06:40.900
Tyler flees to the fair and Chucky makes him
go into this dark ride called The Devil’s

00:06:40.900 --> 00:06:44.800
Lair, and let me just say, THIS is an AWESOME
looking ride.

00:06:44.800 --> 00:06:47.750
This is way above the quality I would expect
from a carnival attraction.

00:06:47.750 --> 00:06:49.860
This is some Haunted Mansion level ****.

00:06:49.860 --> 00:06:54.289
Part 1 of the ride is in a graveyard, representing
Chucky’s numerous victims over the three

00:06:54.289 --> 00:06:55.289
films.

00:06:55.289 --> 00:06:59.360
Part 2 takes place in hell, representing Andy’s
personal hell of once again being hunted by

00:06:59.360 --> 00:07:01.940
Chucky after he thought it was over 8 years
ago.

00:07:01.940 --> 00:07:05.220
Chucky’s ritual is once again interrupted
when he dives out of the way because he doesn’t

00:07:05.220 --> 00:07:08.449
want to be seen by the people on the ride,
but honestly I don’t know why.

00:07:08.449 --> 00:07:11.949
He’s basically no different than an animatronic
-- he’d fit right here.

00:07:11.949 --> 00:07:15.710
Then he gets his face sliced open by this
reaper’s scythe… you know because, they

00:07:15.710 --> 00:07:18.389
used a real scythe to decorate this ride.

00:07:18.389 --> 00:07:22.229
But that doesn’t stop him from making one
more attempt to take over Tyler’s body,

00:07:22.229 --> 00:07:25.880
during which Andy shoots him and blows off
his right arms, something that happens to

00:07:25.880 --> 00:07:27.300
Chucky in all three movies.

00:07:27.300 --> 00:07:31.170
After that, Andy shoots him in the heart,
which makes sense because that’s what worked

00:07:31.170 --> 00:07:35.680
in the first movie, but apparently that just
doesn’t work anymore, cause, you know.

00:07:35.680 --> 00:07:37.220
CONTINUITY.

00:07:37.229 --> 00:07:41.419
So the key this time is to knock Chucky into
a high speed fan and let it shred him up,

00:07:41.419 --> 00:07:44.889
and the shot symbolically represents Chucky
falling into the pits of hell.

00:07:44.889 --> 00:07:47.449
The movie ends on another symbolic shot.

00:07:47.449 --> 00:07:51.479
It’s one I was hesitant to bring up in my
video on the second movie: the carousel.

00:07:51.479 --> 00:07:55.660
In the previous video I talked about how the
carousel represents Andy going around and

00:07:55.660 --> 00:07:59.800
around to different homes and never settling
in because Chucky always comes after him and

00:07:59.800 --> 00:08:00.800
ruins it for it for him.

00:08:00.800 --> 00:08:03.319
So he continues to go around this endless
circle.

00:08:03.319 --> 00:08:07.270
The music at the end seems to suggest that
Chucky isn’t done for good, with the carousel

00:08:07.270 --> 00:08:09.430
telling us it’s business as usual for Andy
Barclay.

00:08:09.430 --> 00:08:13.700
That brings us to the conclusion of the original
Child’s Play series -- but we’ve got a

00:08:13.700 --> 00:08:18.040
remake on the way very shortly, so make sure
you subscribe to CZsWorld so you don’t miss out on

00:08:18.050 --> 00:08:22.180
the next episode of Things You Missed where
I’ll be covering the 2019 Child’s Play.

00:08:22.199 --> 00:08:26.810
Make sure you ring the deathbell for notifications
and I’ll see you then, assuming we both

00:08:26.810 --> 00:08:27.320
survive.

